Devices: What Every Workload Can Touch

Host processes see the host's devices directly: there is no container
boundary, no cgroup device program, and no device node provisioning.
A camera on the truck is visible to every workload on the truck, same
as before, now without any rule machinery in between.

The historical cgroup device rules, bundle device nodes, and nodev
placement checks were deleted with the container runtime. If device
isolation returns, it arrives as a new package with its own document,
not as a resurrection of this one.
